摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Drive Autodesk Fusion 360 from DeepSeek Harness (DSH) - 13 MCP tools including arbitrary Fusion API Python. Vibe-coded end to end by DSH; every modelling command measured against closed-form volumes.","id":"gh:1390842937","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"dsh-fusion360","slug":"Leaveing00001/dsh-fusion360","topics":["addin","autodesk-fusion360","cad","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","fusion360","mcp","mcp-server","parametric-modeling","python","vibecoding"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Drive Autodesk Fusion 360 from DeepSeek Harness (DSH) - 13 MCP tools including arbitrary Fusion API "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"Python. Vibe-coded end to end by DSH; every modelling command measured against closed-form volumes."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-fusion360"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Drive Autodesk Fusion 360 from DeepSeek Harness.** Query the model, change\nparameters, export file"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"s, and run arbitrary Fusion API Python — from a chat."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"中文说明 · Install · Verification · Fusion API notes · DSH compatibility"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> ## 🐋 This is a DeepSeek Harness VibeCoding artifact\n>\n> This project was **vibe-coded end to end b"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"y DeepSeek Harness (DSH)**. Nobody\n> wrote it by hand and then handed it to an agent to tidy up: the"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" agent built it\n> in conversation, driving a live Fusion 360 through **the very bridge it was\n> stil"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"l writing**.\n>\n> Concretely, the agent:\n>\n> - read DSH's own installed application tree and Fusion's"},{"id":"p5s5","text":" shipped Python type\n>   stubs to learn the two APIs instead of trusting its memory of them;\n> - wro"},{"id":"p5s6","text":"te the Fusion add-in, the MCP server, and three test harnesses;\n> - installed the add-in into Fusion"},{"id":"p5s7","text":", restarted DSH, and then called its own tools\n>   back through the MCP layer;\n> - drove **15 modell"},{"id":"p5s8","text":"ing commands** against real Fusion and checked each result\n>   against its closed-form volume, rathe"},{"id":"p5s9","text":"r than settling for \"the call did not\n>   raise\" — see the measured table;\n> - hit **17 places where"},{"id":"p5s10","text":" its recall of the Fusion API disagreed with reality**,\n>   and corrected every one from the actual "},{"id":"p5s11","text":"error text. Those are written up in\n>   Fusion API notes.\n>\n> The mistakes are documented rather tha"},{"id":"p5s12","text":"n hidden, because they are the useful\n> part: most of them fail **silently** in Fusion's API — a cha"},{"id":"p5s13","text":"mfer that produces\n> a healthy feature and changes nothing, a sketch that quietly absorbs a circle\n>"},{"id":"p5s14","text":" as a hole. If you are writing Fusion API code yourself, that page will save you\n> a day.\n>\n> The pr"},{"id":"p5s15","text":"ose in this README is the agent's too. Every number in it is a\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## What it is"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Fusion 360 has **no headless mode**. Any modelling operation needs a running\nFusion instance, and th"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"e Fusion API is single-threaded — it may only be called\nfrom Fusion's primary thread. So a plain MCP"},{"id":"p7s3","text":" server that shells out to Python\ncannot work. This is a two-part bridge:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"The MCP server runs as an ordinary DSH-spawned subprocess. The add-in runs\n*inside* Fusion, joins th"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"e socket requests back onto Fusion's primary thread with\na `CustomEvent`, and executes them there."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Fusion 360 | A desktop install that can run add-ins — verified on **2705.1.15**. Fusion has no hea"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"dless mode, so nothing here works without the app running. |\n| DSH Desktop | Verified on **2.0.17** "},{"id":"p11s3","text":"(2.0.9 also worked). See DSH compatibility. |\n| Python | 3.8+ for the MCP server. **Standard library"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" only** — no `mcp` wheel, no `pip install`. |\n| OS | Windows, verified. The bridge itself is plain s"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"tdlib and the manifest declares `windows\\|mac`, but nothing here has been run on macOS. The helpers "},{"id":"p11s6","text":"in `tools/` are PowerShell and `.bat`, so those are Windows-only. |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"> **The install is two-part and `npm` cannot complete it.** `package.json`\n> declares `dsh.bundle.pa"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"tch` — the DSH-side half, which is the cordis patch in\n> `dsh/cordis.patch.yml` — but the other half"},{"id":"p14s3","text":" is an add-in\n> that has to be copied into *Fusion's* AddIns folder, which no package manager\n> can "},{"id":"p14s4","text":"do for you. There is deliberately no `postinstall` script reaching into\n> another application's dire"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"ctories; the two commands above are the install. The\n> npm manifest exists so plugin catalogs can id"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"entify this repo, which is why it\n> is marked `\"private\": true` and not published."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Ask DSH to call `mcp__fusion360__fusion_status`. A healthy reply:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Full walkthrough, including the manual add-in path and troubleshooting:\n**docs/install.md**."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### Prove it works"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"`examples/build_a_part.py` builds a 100 × 60 × 8 mm\nplate with four R6 corner rounds and four ⌀4.5 t"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"hrough holes, and checks its own\nvolume at every stage — 48000 → 47752.78 → **47243.84 mm³**. Run it"},{"id":"p19s3","text":" as the `code`\nargument of `mcp__fusion360__fusion_run_python` and it either matches or raises."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"It is the fastest way to tell a working install from a broken one, and it is\nworth reading as an exa"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"mple of the API's sharp edges being handled: profile\nselection by bounding box, the sketch-frame con"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"version, and the chamfer's\n`isTangentChain` trap are all commented in place."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Tools"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Thirteen tools, exposed to DSH as `mcp__fusion360__<name>`."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| Tool | Purpose |"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| `fusion_status` | Reachability, Fusion version, signed-in user |\n| `fusion_document_info` | Active"},{"id":"p24s2","text":" design: units, body/parameter counts, bounding box |\n| `fusion_list_bodies` | Every body with volum"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"e (mm³), area (mm²), bbox, material |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## What actually works"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Every command below was driven through `fusion_run_python` against a live Fusion\n**2705.1.15** and c"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"hecked against the closed-form volume. These are measurements,\nnot smoke tests."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| Command | Measured | Analytic |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"| Sketch: rectangle, circle, arc, fitted spline | 8 curves, 3 closed profiles | — |\n| Extrude, new b"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"ody 60 × 40 × 10 | 24000.00 mm³ | 24000 |\n| Extrude, join — boss ⌀16 × 16 | +3216.99 mm³ | +3216.99 "},{"id":"p28s3","text":"|\n| Extrude, cut through-all — ⌀10 | −785.40 mm³ | −785.40 |\n| Fillet, 4 vertical edges R3 | −77.26 "},{"id":"p28s4","text":"mm³ | −77.26 |\n| Chamfer, 4 top edges 1 mm | −98.67 mm³, 6 → 10 faces | −100 |\n| Loft, ⌀40 → ⌀16 ove"},{"id":"p28s5","text":"r 30 mm | 19603.54 mm³ | 19603.54 |\n| Revolve, rectangle about Z, 360° | 42411.50 mm³ | 42411.50 |\n|"},{"id":"p28s6","text":" Sweep, ⌀10 circle along a 50 mm line | 3926.99 mm³ | 3926.99 |\n| Shell, top face open, 2 mm wall | "},{"id":"p28s7","text":"7872.00 mm³ | 7872 |\n| Hole ⌀4.5 through 8 mm | −127.23 mm³ | −127.23 |\n| Rectangular pattern 2 × 2 "},{"id":"p28s8","text":"| 47491.06 mm³, 4 holes | 47491.06 |\n| Full part: plate + R6 + 4 × ⌀4.5 | 48000.00 → 47752.78 → 4724"},{"id":"p28s9","text":"3.84 | same |\n| Sketch on a solid face + blind cut | 23547.61 mm³ | 23547.61 |"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The chamfer's shortfall against a naive `area × length` figure is the corner\ntreatment where four ch"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"amfers meet — it reproduces on a plain box (98.667 vs\n100 mm³), so it is geometry, not error."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Full tables, including the MCP-layer round trip and the STL/STEP export checks:\n**docs/verification."},{"id":"p30s2","text":"tables, including the MCP-layer round trip and the STL/STEP export checks:\n**docs/verification.md**."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
